#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096419 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f570287d-b0e4-53bb-8fa1-37348ca9202f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Differential Equation Using Integration"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8b9014e-32cf-5f04-856c-7fd663bea50f" :question/math-academy-id "e-528" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $f'(x) - 3\\sin(2x) = 0.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\nf'(x) = 3\\sin{2x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =3\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096420 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a8e6c58c-da62-5dab-8325-a53c14d9b8ba" :question/math-academy-id "e-529" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d^2 y}{\\textrm d x^2} = x.\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+C)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3}+Cx+D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$ We cannot combine them, because $C$ is being multiplied by $x$ while $D$ is not."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096421 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23789a74-f1e3-5e26-8678-21f84a11a12b" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution Curves of a Differential Equation"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ab40a4d3-c418-5b64-a04c-bb017155a4d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-530" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $y'  = 2x,$ and sketch the solution curves of this equation." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\ny = x^2+C.\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011667/assets/e37771799ef5fadc259e6ea0073042a83e0974b5a2619d1af3e87a7467e6d780.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096422 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Differential Equation With a Given Condition"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29a0265e-ad88-5ac9-88fe-878aa4f0d0bf" :question/math-academy-id "e-531" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $f(0)=2.$\n\n$$\nf'(x) - \\dfrac{3}{1+x^2} = 0\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\nf'(x) = \\dfrac{3}{1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{3}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =3\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $f(x) = 3\\arctan{x} + C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0) = 2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C \\\\ 2 & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)+C \\\\ 2 & =0+C \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is \n\n$$\nf(x)=3\\arctan x + 2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289746 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f570287d-b0e4-53bb-8fa1-37348ca9202f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Differential Equation Using Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe1ffa70-41ba-592d-9221-889fddb97a61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289748} {:answer/id #uuid "5e89e576-486a-554f-a8e4-561e6e58ad62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289749} {:answer/id #uuid "abe66a86-26ba-52ce-ae99-cda0b40a5423" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289750} {:answer/id #uuid "d68943c3-babc-5cca-bb4a-6060331890a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289751} {:answer/id #uuid "f7d5de22-29dc-571a-9a04-6e24438dc027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e89e576-486a-554f-a8e4-561e6e58ad62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289749} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f4971da-77d9-5b10-9742-4958f510bb24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae4d3203-76af-57e6-914e-e9a022b4a7ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-119032" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the derivative term is already isolated on the left:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289760 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f570287d-b0e4-53bb-8fa1-37348ca9202f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Differential Equation Using Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5df53c4f-461b-58da-b708-fe15732e2635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289762} {:answer/id #uuid "8adbc7d2-6f0c-5a4b-8810-f0c4038f4edd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)={x}^{2}(2x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289763} {:answer/id #uuid "4ab4224b-f455-5ab1-8988-6720dea5f79b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)={x}^{2}(2-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289764} {:answer/id #uuid "5d634642-3a2b-5db5-8bf9-7acfea5de072" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(3-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289765} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf1bfe2-3b08-5429-a12d-2fdcda9de7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cf1bfe2-3b08-5429-a12d-2fdcda9de7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289766} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b665f02-3442-53c7-bbf5-d87277631ced" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "36c02825-1f2e-5058-9fc1-074753d8120c" :question/math-academy-id "q-119035" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)+6{x}^{2}=4x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =4x-6{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4x-6{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3}+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}(1-x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289781 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f76c7bc8-5f0f-5691-b0f5-d5e342b0537e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{4}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289783} {:answer/id #uuid "38ff9b99-6f09-5946-b632-57cf62d75cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{4}-5{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289784} {:answer/id #uuid "e0a27261-a5ca-518c-8c7b-d480e13742a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289785} {:answer/id #uuid "76c484bc-cbc4-5551-a1f8-91f030aab2ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289786} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc024df-0d20-5b15-bcc3-a94f7517d89f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-4{x}^{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76c484bc-cbc4-5551-a1f8-91f030aab2ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289786} :answer-field/id #uuid "15d4af72-1848-578c-907a-e3c3e65ecc24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75c31897-52bd-540c-a546-ce6303ed7371" :question/math-academy-id "q-119043" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+5=6{x}^{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=6{x}^{2}-5.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-5)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-5x+C \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}-5x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2{x}^{3}-5x+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})-5(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{2}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289788 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Differential Equation With a Given Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d14e0df1-3bb8-5197-b25c-bc87e8eef3d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289790} {:answer/id #uuid "4f766d19-73fe-5c00-851c-def3a95b1697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289791} {:answer/id #uuid "b25c8c97-b577-5dfa-9d6d-9b976fd446bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289792} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb0664d-836b-5d5d-aeb4-68ec1251deba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289793} {:answer/id #uuid "73d0e6bb-117a-5547-ad15-e6a24ca686e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f766d19-73fe-5c00-851c-def3a95b1697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289791} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9fb5778-ba1b-563c-934c-4d2eafdbb97b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a18f6dbb-80c9-5e0a-b091-fdf4e8634a66" :question/math-academy-id "q-119045" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${f}^{′}(x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ that satisfies the condition $f(0)=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =-2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $f(0)=-1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+C \\\\ -1 & =-2(0)+C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292742 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23789a74-f1e3-5e26-8678-21f84a11a12b" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution Curves of a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd7fb28d-d2af-5809-9602-c6c9c61aa684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/d7ecaa30c600519d6bfcc7a43a4275a55d6f6cc1b52b48c8e7b117e7a772343e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292744} {:answer/id #uuid "476b9b70-6126-5f8b-b65b-3ddd79e11fcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/8ede6d26a62570f4037ecc58c377e95389ab00dbee36b60c46e6fb2021e01cea.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292745} {:answer/id #uuid "0252ec44-9753-55db-bbb2-be4dbfeaaa45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/cece096a5b267821994e9b6d8142f0d7ea684bbe8e28da7cdb01b87a73f1db4c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292746} {:answer/id #uuid "ae440fff-25e4-5f3f-841f-9ccae733397a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/96359fe35288b866cbf9fd929e2515af04a4ec0dc565a4cd4af9d3a8fcd20f94.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292747} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccca60c-7f65-5eec-8bf7-fb08e7594b1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/7832a2110292cb364cf06c24eb51e9bb1ee42fe430ac8fcc381af047a09125e4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd7fb28d-d2af-5809-9602-c6c9c61aa684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/d7ecaa30c600519d6bfcc7a43a4275a55d6f6cc1b52b48c8e7b117e7a772343e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292744} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d5b2ef1-c08b-50ea-a722-b5ebadbae937" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292743}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "370a4996-fe99-533f-b6a9-5042b61aa194" :question/math-academy-id "q-119132" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{e}^{-x/4}}{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{e}^{-x/4}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{-x/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-4{e}^{-x/4}) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-x/4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=0,3,6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/a4b534bd33daabc94aa3c86935b1fd4c0be723fafbc418ed382716541a864293.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Differential Equation With a Given Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be185d95-e478-5395-97f2-47a81ca133e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9-\\frac{8}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be185d95-e478-5395-97f2-47a81ca133e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9-\\frac{8}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292751} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdaa6dac-352d-59d2-a0be-00d8b5580145" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d86030f5-75e2-57ba-94c6-7a636a2e8eeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-352066" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(x-3)^{2}{y}^{′}=8$ that satisfies the condition $y(4)=1.$\n\n$y=\\,${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =8\\int \\frac{1}{(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8(-\\frac{1}{x-3})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{x-3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-\\frac{8}{x-3}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(4)=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-\\frac{8}{4-3}+C \\\\ 1 & =-8+C \\\\ C & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{8}{x-3}+9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f570287d-b0e4-53bb-8fa1-37348ca9202f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Differential Equation Using Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "991a4d75-b082-5ddb-9e0e-daec82c04821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-2e^{2x} - x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095672} {:answer/id #uuid "b018b6ae-1940-5995-bcd3-0cb355cdfdbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-4e^{2x} - 2x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095673} {:answer/id #uuid "c2357d5d-526c-504c-b3d2-09cc85042828" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-e^{2x} - x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095674} {:answer/id #uuid "eed6b0a7-f89a-5f99-8fa6-663cdc54a4e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-e^{2x} - 2x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095675} {:answer/id #uuid "5a53ae9e-07c4-5848-85e2-a1c6b214ea93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-2e^{2x} - 2x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "991a4d75-b082-5ddb-9e0e-daec82c04821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-2e^{2x} - x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095672} :answer-field/id #uuid "144fd343-32aa-51c0-ba1c-2d78f454b0d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cb82aa2f-3e4a-523a-94c2-c95aa3cb8ffa" :question/math-academy-id "q-50136" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{e}^{2x}=-2x.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{2x}-2x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}y & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2x}-{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097222 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23789a74-f1e3-5e26-8678-21f84a11a12b" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution Curves of a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "853aeea8-65f0-5fb9-8258-80667aea2abd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50195-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095690} {:answer/id #uuid "a94dc35e-7f42-58d5-bacb-d6ebe1a5ec26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50195-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095691} {:answer/id #uuid "efb18e51-9c8d-5683-8dc6-f9dd9a0e7082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50195-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095692} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9b1208-989e-52fe-9319-003ca0fe7916" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50195-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095693} {:answer/id #uuid "3c3f4a30-dc1d-5668-a728-9b3bc043b41c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50195-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a94dc35e-7f42-58d5-bacb-d6ebe1a5ec26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1061/Source/Images/q-50195-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095691} :answer-field/id #uuid "baa5bcf1-a2e1-5611-80a8-e28d46985c9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a33d5262-3afa-580b-b512-aba7c2576e69" :question/math-academy-id "q-50195" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2(x - 1)$?" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Integrating $y'=2(x-1)$ gives\n$$y=(x-1)^2+C.$$\nThe solution curves are upward-opening parabolas, all with symmetry axis $x=1$, differing only by vertical translation. Select the diagram showing this family; its vertices all have $x$-coordinate $1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23789a74-f1e3-5e26-8678-21f84a11a12b" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution Curves of a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b3b2036-4273-53bc-aa24-a885d6e03696" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/757072d5f7b2edaf1eb22e3e1a1c4135a387293396c9a4213ee3a2e213102ee6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292761} {:answer/id #uuid "feb6948b-da9f-5926-9102-61f011a1fa4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/bec2fa9f6c2673fe9bc71fbdadb8f2cbf4c37ef05a38dd2486be3fac7e2b98d2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292762} {:answer/id #uuid "295d0262-efca-5cce-bbd2-71fd6d150f1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference